import{H as e,ht as t,nt as n,tt as r}from"./chunks/framework.CXX_0q1Z.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Attributes and Skills","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/modules/accessory/integration.md","filePath":"en/modules/accessory/integration.md","lastUpdated":0}`),a={name:`en/modules/accessory/integration.md`};function o(e,i,a,o,s,c){return t(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[n(`<h1 id="attributes-and-skills" tabindex="-1">Attributes and Skills <a class="header-anchor" href="#attributes-and-skills" aria-label="Permalink to “Attributes and Skills”">​</a></h1><p>Accessory attributes and skills are not computed by EmakiAccessory itself; they are registered into the public extension points of EmakiAttribute and EmakiSkills. Both are optional dependencies, so the corresponding half simply switches off when one is absent while the accessory panel keeps working.</p><h2 id="attributes-into-emakiattribute" tabindex="-1">Attributes into EmakiAttribute <a class="header-anchor" href="#attributes-into-emakiattribute" aria-label="Permalink to “Attributes into EmakiAttribute”">​</a></h2><p>EmakiAccessory registers a <strong>contribution provider</strong> with EmakiAttribute (provider id <code>emakiaccessory:accessories</code>, priority 100), feeding accessory attributes in as a distinct source. It registers no custom equipment slot and writes nothing onto the player&#39;s vanilla attributes.</p><p>The reported source ids:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Source id</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>emakiaccessory:accessory</code></td><td>Attributes of an individual accessory.</td></tr><tr><td><code>emakiaccessory:set</code></td><td>Accessory set bonuses.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Attribute values are read through EmakiAttribute&#39;s <code>AttributeCatalog#itemSnapshot</code> — <strong>the same parser the equipment path uses</strong>. An accessory and a helmet carrying identical data therefore produce identical numbers, and parent-attribute expansion plus range-spread companion keys come along with it.</p><p>Range-spread companion keys are summed like any other key; otherwise a ranged accessory would keep its lower bound and lose its spread.</p><p>When EmakiAttribute is unavailable (<code>EmakiAttributeApi.status().usable()</code> is false) no provider is registered, so accessories grant no attributes at all.</p><h2 id="skills-into-emakiskills" tabindex="-1">Skills into EmakiSkills <a class="header-anchor" href="#skills-into-emakiskills" aria-label="Permalink to “Skills into EmakiSkills”">​</a></h2><p>EmakiAccessory registers a <strong>skill source</strong> with EmakiSkills (provider id <code>accessories</code>). Equipment skill payloads on an accessory are read by <code>AccessorySkillPayloadCodec.read</code>, the same PDC contract Item, Forge, Gem and Strengthen write.</p><p>Skills listed in an accessory set&#39;s <code>thresholds[].effects[].es_skills</code> take effect through that same path.</p><p>The source-slot field of each skill entry is the <strong>slot instance id</strong> for single-accessory skills and <code>set:&lt;setId&gt;</code> for set skills.</p><p>With EmakiSkills absent the module still enables normally: <code>AccessoryProviderRegistrar</code> loads the integration class reflectively by name (<code>emaki.jiuwu.craft.accessory.provider.AccessorySkillsProviderIntegration</code>) and only does so while <code>EmakiSkills</code> is enabled, so a missing EmakiSkills cannot fail class loading — there is simply no skill source.</p><h2 id="slot-restriction-criterion" tabindex="-1">Slot Restriction Criterion <a class="header-anchor" href="#slot-restriction-criterion" aria-label="Permalink to “Slot Restriction Criterion”">​</a></h2><p>Accessories support <code>active_slot</code> declarations just like equipment. The accessory side collects &quot;the slots the item declares&quot; into one set, unioned from:</p><ol><li>the <code>active_slot</code> metadata of every EmakiAttribute attribute payload (EmakiItem writes <code>all</code> when the item declares no equipment slot; a missing metadata value contributes nothing);</li><li>the active_slot of the EmakiSkills skill payload (which contributes at least <code>all</code> whenever the payload exists);</li><li>the optional <code>slot_sources.pdc</code> and <code>slot_sources.lore</code> sources from <code>config.yml</code>.</li></ol><p>The matching rule: the item passes as soon as <strong>any single declaration hits the current cell</strong> (any-of). Note this is <strong>not</strong> the all-of rule of EmakiAttribute&#39;s equipment path (where any unmatched declaration drops the whole item&#39;s contribution); the accessory side is a separate implementation because <code>itemSnapshot</code> performs no slot filtering while the equipment path&#39;s gate is internal to EmakiAttribute.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>The item&#39;s declared slot</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>all</code></td><td>Active in any accessory slot.</td></tr><tr><td>A part id, such as <code>ring</code></td><td>Active in any cell of that part (the accessory side accepts this bare part id form).</td></tr><tr><td>A slot instance id, such as <code>ring_1</code></td><td>Active only in that cell.</td></tr><tr><td>Anything else (such as the equipment slot names <code>hand</code> or <code>main_hand</code>)</td><td>Hits no accessory slot, i.e. inactive.</td></tr><tr><td>An empty set (no <code>active_slot</code>, no skill payload, and neither optional source readable)</td><td>Inactive: the item&#39;s attribute and skill contributions are dropped entirely.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>If the equipment-side rules ever change, this accessory-side implementation must be re-evaluated.</p><h2 id="when-recomputation-happens" tabindex="-1">When Recomputation Happens <a class="header-anchor" href="#when-recomputation-happens" aria-label="Permalink to “When Recomputation Happens”">​</a></h2><p>Contribution snapshots are recomputed when accessory contents change: a GUI edit, a completed data load, a reload, a <code>/eacc retrieve</code>, or a death drop that clears the enabled page. Opening the window without changing anything does not recompute.</p><p>Recomputation deliberately <strong>does not happen inside the provider callback</strong>. EmakiAttribute&#39;s combat snapshot collector calls the contribution provider while computing its cache signature, meaning the provider runs on every combat snapshot read; parsing PDC there would put item deserialisation on the combat hot path.</p><h2 id="threading" tabindex="-1">Threading <a class="header-anchor" href="#threading" aria-label="Permalink to “Threading”">​</a></h2><p>Recomputation must run on the owner thread of the player holding the items: the attribute parser writes its result back into item PDC as a cache, so it is not safe off-thread.</p><h2 id="behaviour-with-modules-missing" tabindex="-1">Behaviour With Modules Missing <a class="header-anchor" href="#behaviour-with-modules-missing" aria-label="Permalink to “Behaviour With Modules Missing”">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Missing module</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>EmakiAttribute</td><td>No attribute provider is registered, so accessories grant no attributes; the panel and set piece counting keep working (set counting depends on EmakiItem only).</td></tr><tr><td>EmakiSkills</td><td>No skill source is registered, so neither accessory nor set skills are granted; everything else keeps working.</td></tr><tr><td>EmakiItem</td><td><code>unique</code> deduplication falls back to vanilla material matching and stays active; accessory sets relying on <code>pieces[].item</code> are entirely inactive (their piece count stays 0).</td></tr><tr><td>PlaceholderAPI</td><td>PAPI placeholders in text are no longer replaced and pass through unchanged.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>EmakiAccessory itself has <strong>no</strong> PlaceholderAPI expansion and exposes no <code>%emakiaccessory_*%</code> placeholders; it only consumes PlaceholderAPI optionally. The module also registers <strong>no</strong> actions into the CoreLib action registry (the module&#39;s only <code>super(&quot;accessory&quot;, …)</code> is the config-precheck contributor&#39;s module id, not an action segment).</p>`,28)]])}var s=e(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};